  <iati-identifier>XI-IATI-EC_NEAR-2022-ACT-61469</iati-identifier>
  <reporting-org ref="XI-IATI-EC_NEAR" secondary-reporter="0" type="15">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">European Commission - Directorate-General for Neighbourhood and Enlargement Negotiations</narrative>
  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">EU4 PAR Increased Administrative Capacity - BA2022AAP</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This Action will support the further implementation of the PAR Strategic Framework and more precisely country&#xbf;s willingness to respond positively to its citizens greater expectations from the public administration regarding the quality, speed, price, transparency and accessibility of services it delivers, at the same time contributing to harmonized modernisation of public administration observing EU accession criteria. The action will develop a mechanism for online collaborative use of software tools facilitating the development of the digital economy to be utilised by society as a whole, through piloting sectors as clearly proposed in the PAR Strategic Framework. In the area of statistics, the Action will contribute to further harmonization and modernisation of BiH statistics with EU standards, volume and quality of data using relevant administrative sources as well as gender mainstreaming approach. In addition, the Action will improve finance statistics by digitalization and modernization of statistical production in Central Bank. The intervention will deliver concrete countrywide sustainable results in line with national strategies and national priorities. The Action as such is fully in line with IPA III PF and SDG 16, where both underpin strong institutions, development of modernised public administrations at all levels of government as well as strengthening statistical systems which are of utmost importance for evidence-based decision-making. Finally, the action contributes to the implementation of Key Priority 14 by supporting establishment of quicker, cheaper, more transparent and more accessible public services which are cornerstones for better functioning public administration.</narrative>
  </description>
